{#
    A page of the public site in the theme layout it uses (`layout_template`). The blocks are rendered by their
    types, which escape everything they print, so they are printed as they are. `head`, the HTML the modules listening
    to PublicPageRendering escaped, is printed by core's head partial (`@seo/head.html.twig`), which every theme's
    shell includes.
    Context: `layout_template`, `title`, `lead` (the summary, optional), `locale`, `site_name`, `content`, `head`,
    `updated_at` (UTC), and whatever the modules added (`main_menu`, `footer_menu`, `breadcrumbs` …). `hero` is HTML a
    module escaped for the `hero` block of layouts that have one (`home`), such as the Download button on a theme's
    preview page.
#}
{% extends layout_template %}
{% block hero %}{{ hero|default('')|raw }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}{{ content|raw }}{% endblock %}
